Sheet 2 — Configuration ⚠️ Re-run this

Your Sheet2 still has the original ten columns. The new query didn't take — most likely the paste broke, or Excel reopened the earlier CSV.

Here's a simplified version. I've removed the calculated fields, because doing those in Excel is more reliable than fighting KQL:


resources
| where type == "microsoft.sql/servers/databases" and name != "master"
| extend server = tostring(split(id,'/')[8])
| project
    resourceGroup,
    server,
    name,
    status = tostring(properties.status),
    tier = tostring(sku.tier),
    skuName = tostring(sku.name),
    capacity = toint(sku.capacity),
    minCapacity = todouble(properties.minCapacity),
    autoPauseDelay = toint(properties.autoPauseDelay),
    maxSizeBytes = tolong(properties.maxSizeBytes),
    licenseType = tostring(properties.licenseType),
    backupRedundancy = tostring(properties.currentBackupStorageRedundancy),
    zoneRedundant = tostring(properties.zoneRedundant),
    readScale = tostring(properties.readScale),
    elasticPoolId = tostring(properties.elasticPoolId),
    createdTime = todatetime(properties.creationDate),
    earliestRestore = todatetime(properties.earliestRestoreDate),
    tagsText = tostring(tags)
| order by capacity desc



